{
  "_name": "t34_channel_spam_origin",
  "_desc": "Channel anti-spam: per-origin COUNT throttle (ROADMAP 3). spammer floods channel 7 (24 posts); channels expose the origin (channel_msg_id high byte) so every node caps DISTINCT msgs per origin. Test sets channel_origin_max_per_window=3 (production default 20) to exercise the mechanism in a short contended run -- same pattern as t33b tightening the duty budget. relay (1st hop) decodes the spammers broadcasts, counts the origin, and after 3 SILENTLY drops the rest (channel_drop_originator_throttle): not buffered -> never advertised/pulled/re-broadcast. edge (2 hops, hears only relays gossip) sees only the admitted head -> amplification contained mesh-wide. Verifies: (1) >=1 channel_drop_originator_throttle at relay (teeth); (2) >=1 channel_msg_received at edge (early msgs propagate -> rate-limit not all-drop).",
